Introduction to Spring Boot:
Spring Framework is an open source java framework developed by
Rod Johnson. It provides infrastructure support for developing
Java application.

"Write less code and focus more on the business logic"

Spring boot is an extension of spring framework.

It helps developer to build :

i)Web application(MVC)
ii)REST API
iii)Enterprise Application
iv)Microservices
v)Cloud Apps
vi)Batch App

Why was Spring introduced?
J2EE
EJB - Enterprise Java Beans

Problems with EJB:

i)complex XML configuration
ii)Difficult to deploy
iii)Heavyweight framework
iv)Tight Coupling
v)Hard to test
vi)Poor maintainability

Coupling: Interdependency between modules.


Spring solved these issues by introducing:
i)Lightweight architecture
ii)Dependency Injection
iii)Inversion Of control(IOC)
iv)POJO based programming(Plain Old Java Objects)
v)Easy testing
vi)Modular architecture(Core, Context, Beans, MVC, AOP, Data, Security)




